# Mobile API auth

- Content GET routes require `Authorization: Bearer` only. Never accept `X-TR-App-Key` on content routes.
- Only `POST /auth/token` may use `X-TR-App-Key` to mint short-lived tokens.
- If `tr_mobile_app_key` is empty, the API must fail closed (`503`). Do not restore open-by-default access.
- Keep page/limit caps (`limit` ≤ 20, posts page ≤ 50, search page ≤ 10). Do not remove without an equivalent abuse control.
- Do not run `the_content` on API bodies; keep `wp_kses_post` (or tighter) for mobile HTML.
- Password-protected posts must not appear in list/detail/search.
- Origin rate limiting is best-effort; document Cloudflare as the real DDoS control. Do not claim the App Key makes clone apps impossible.
